body="""
## Why DHA files get looked at more closely
DHA Lahore is one of the most data-rich addresses in the country from FBR's point of view. Every plot and house transfer goes through the DHA transfer office, which collects the buyer's and seller's advance tax and reports the transaction. Vehicles are registered against CNICs with Excise, banks report large deposits and profit payments, and electricity bills for big houses are available to FBR through the distribution company. None of this is secret, and FBR's systems now join it together automatically.

So the risk for a DHA resident is rarely that FBR "doesn't know" something. It is that the return says one thing and the third-party data says another. A salaried executive who files only the salary certificate, while a plot purchase sits in DHA's records under the same CNIC, has created a mismatch even if every rupee was honestly earned.

## The three mismatches we see most often in DHA
- **Property bought in one year, money shown in another.** The 236K advance tax at transfer appears in your tax profile for the year of transfer. If the wealth statement for that year does not show the plot or house — or shows it without the funds that paid for it — the wealth reconciliation breaks.
- **Family assets in the wrong name.** Houses bought in a spouse's or child's name, funded by the main earner, need either a separate return for that person or a clear gift trail in the earner's statement.
- **Foreign spending without foreign income.** School and university fees paid abroad, credit card spending on travel, and remittances to children studying overseas all point to a level of spending the return should support.

## What a clean DHA return actually contains
The fix is not complicated, but it has to be done in the right order. We start from the wealth statement, not the income form, because that is where DHA households usually go wrong.

1. List every immovable property by its DHA plot or house number, with acquisition date and cost, including files that have not yet been allotted a plot.
2. Match each acquisition to its source — salary savings, business profit, sale of an earlier property, gift, inheritance or loan.
3. Pull the advance tax already deducted (property transfers, vehicle registration, bank profit, electricity) from your FBR profile so none of it is wasted.
4. Only then prepare the income side, so that income plus other inflows minus household expenses lands exactly on your closing wealth.

> If you have bought or sold anything in DHA in the last two tax years and did not file a wealth statement that year, do not wait for a Section 111 or 116 notice. A revised return filed voluntarily is far easier to defend than one filed under notice.

## Property transfer tax rates DHA buyers and sellers should know
DHA collects advance income tax on every transfer on FBR's behalf. For transfers registered from 1 July 2026, the rates on the current schedule are:

| Who pays | Section | Active filer | Not on ATL |
| Buyer | 236K | 1.25% | 2.5% |
| Seller | 236C | 2.75% | 5.5% |

These are calculated on the higher of FBR's valuation and the declared value, and for filers they are adjustable against the year's actual tax liability. Capital gains tax on the sale itself is worked out separately in the return and depends on how long you held the property and when you acquired it. Our [property transfer tax guide](/blogs/property-transfer-tax-2026-27-pakistan-236c-236k) walks through the arithmetic.

## Where the dedicated DHA pages come in
DHA is not one neighbourhood — Phase 1's older houses, Phase 3's Y Block shops, Phase 6's commercial offices and the newer sectors around Rahbar and Phase 9 all produce very different tax files. Each phase page below covers the issue we see most among clients from that part of DHA, so use the one closest to your situation.
""",
